      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "UNRWA USA exhibits institutional-grade accountability, evidenced by its <cite id=\"12\">91/100 rating from Charity Navigator</cite>. This includes a <cite id=\"14\">perfect 100 score for Leadership</cite>, reflecting a clear strategic vision and strong board oversight. The organization manages <cite id=\"15\">3.9 months of working capital</cite>, providing a resilient financial cushion for its large-scale operations. Their commitment to transparency is further validated by their <cite id=\"13\">Platinum Seal from Candid</cite>, the highest level of disclosure available for non-profit outcomes."
      ],
      "summary": "UNRWA USA National Committee serves as a vital lifeline for Palestine refugees, focusing on education, healthcare, and emergency relief. The organization demonstrates a high level of financial efficiency, reporting that <cite id=\"1\">93.4% of its spending</cite> was directed to programs in FY2024. This performance significantly exceeds the <cite id=\"2\">75% industry standard</cite> for non-profits. In FY2024, the charity reported <cite id=\"3\">$51,495,126 in total revenue</cite>, representing a massive <cite id=\"4\">3-year revenue CAGR of 206.6%</cite>. This rapid growth reflects the urgent humanitarian needs in Gaza and the West Bank. The organization maintains <cite id=\"5\">extremely low fundraising costs</cite>, spending only <cite id=\"6\">$0.05 to raise every $1</cite>. This lean operation ensures that the vast majority of contributions reach the field. Beyond emergency aid, the charity funds <cite id=\"7\">university and post-graduate scholarships</cite> and supports <cite id=\"8\">mental health and hospital services</cite>. Their work is deeply integrated with local needs, providing <cite id=\"9\">thousands of food parcels</cite> and repairing <cite id=\"10\">damaged shelters</cite> in conflict zones. For Muslim donors, the organization offers a <cite id=\"11\">verified zakat-eligible giving option</cite>, ensuring funds reach the poor and needy (fuqara and masakin) in accordance with Islamic principles.",
